+  "discoveredDate": "2026-09-21",
+  "id": "ISS-003",
+  "impact": "withRequestId guards a blank id with `requestId.trim() === \"\"` but does not check the type first, so a JS caller (or any boundary where the id arrives untyped, e.g. a header value) gets `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'trim')` for undefined and `TypeError: requestId.trim is not a function` for a number — both verified at HEAD — instead of the intended \"AppLogger requires a non-empty request id\". The logger is the choke point every path funnels through, so the clear message belongs here; T-2 added a `typeof` guard to JobQueue.enqueue, which covers the job path only. Fix: `typeof requestId !== \"string\" || requestId.trim() === \"\"`.",
